data/github/explore/repos/QuagKhai003__assessment/CLAUDE.md-31-- **Official SDK.** Use the official Gemini SDK (JS, since Next.js is JS), not hand-rolled REST unless the SDK lacks an endpoint we need.
data/github/explore/repos/QuagKhai003__assessment/CLAUDE.md-32-- **Send the book once, reuse the result.** Upload the book once (File API) and chain interactions by id (`previous_interaction_id`). Never re-send the full book text on later steps.
data/github/explore/repos/QuagKhai003__assessment/CLAUDE.md-33-- **No auto-retry.** Never retry a failed Gemini call in a loop. Retries are user-triggered only.
data/github/explore/repos/QuagKhai003__assessment/CLAUDE.md:34:- **Key in env var**, never committed. Ship `.env.example`.
data/github/explore/repos/QuagKhai003__assessment/CLAUDE.md-35-- **Caps enforced server-side.** A finished project draws at most **2** character portraits + **1** chapter illustration — the hard, cost-bounding cap on *images* (each image is a paid request). In **Selection** mode the text step may propose a larger candidate *pool* (`CHARACTER_POOL` / `CHAPTER_POOL`, text-only and cheap) to pick from; **Auto** asks for only the capped count. Either way the backend caps the drawn images (`resolveSelection` slices to `MAX_CHARACTERS` / `MAX_CHAPTERS`) — never rely on the UI. The image caps are fixed literals, not tunables.
data/github/explore/repos/QuagKhai003__assessment/CLAUDE.md-36-- **No-content guard.** If the text yields no characters/chapters, the step fails with a "delete this project / start a new one" message — there is no in-project recovery (you can't conjure characters a text lacks). Plus a length pre-check at project creation.
