data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md:42:When a Bukkit/Paper plugin invokes a method on a bridge stub that has no real implementation, the stub MUST call `StubCallLog.logOnce(pluginId, signature)`. On the first hit per `(plugin, signature)` pair, the shared `StubCallLog` emits a WARNING-level JUL line for server operators (server console only). Subsequent hits for the same `(plugin, signature)` are silent.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-43-
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-44-The in-game broadcast sink is intentionally NOT installed by the Bukkit bridge — stub-call warnings stay in the server console so they don't spam every player's chat. When adding or hand-tuning a bridge facade, keep the `StubCallLog.logOnce` call in any method that remains a no-op; do not re-install the broadcast sink without explicit instruction.
