data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-64-
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-65-Whenever new functionality is added (a new feature, new API, new bridge surface, new code path), test coverage is mandatory before the work is closed out. Specifically:
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-66-
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md:67:- After the user confirms the feature works in their manual test, but BEFORE committing or moving to the next feature/task, audit whether tests exist for what was added.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-68-- Both unit tests AND integration tests are required. Unit tests cover the smallest unit (one class, one method, one branch) in isolation; integration tests cover the wiring between units and the broader subsystem (e.g. a bridge listener that the host actually fires, or a Gradle-emitted artifact loading at runtime).
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-69-- Do not add tests speculatively before the user confirms — the design may still change. Add them once the behavior is locked in.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-70-- If a feature genuinely cannot be tested at one of the two levels (e.g. there is no meaningful integration boundary, or the unit is purely declarative), state that explicitly to the user when reporting completion rather than skipping silently.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md:71:- Run the relevant test tasks to confirm the new tests pass before committing.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-72-
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-73-## E2E Test Rules
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-74-
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md:75:- NEVER run two Gradle test suites in parallel. They share the Gradle daemon and will conflict/kill each other. Always run test tasks sequentially — wait for one to complete before starting the next.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-76-- BEFORE launching any Gradle test, ALWAYS check `ps aux | grep -E "testCrossVersion|testLWJGL3|testModern|e2e-xv-|GradleWorker" | grep -v grep` to verify no other test is already running. If one is, stop and ask the user before proceeding.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md-77-- NEVER run a full test suite when only a single test needs to verify a bug fix. Always find a way to run just the specific test in isolation (e.g. create a temporary focused test class, use `--tests` filtering, or add a temporary include to the Gradle task). Delete any temporary test infrastructure after verification.
data/github/explore/repos/martinambrus__RDForward/CLAUDE.md:78:- Do NOT start tests proactively. Only run tests when the user explicitly asks.
--
